WEBVTT

00:07.480 --> 00:10.440
The festival season is 
back for another year.

00:10.440 --> 00:11.600
"Festival"?

00:11.600 --> 00:14.200
It's Flatta's dance festival.

00:14.200 --> 00:16.880
It started about 250 years ago,

00:16.880 --> 00:20.240
and everyone dances however they please 
in the town square or the highlands.

00:20.240 --> 00:23.650
It's about offering the fruits 
of the harvest to the earth god

00:23.650 --> 00:26.240
and praying for a bountiful 
harvest next year.

00:26.670 --> 00:28.770
The event runs for two days,

00:28.770 --> 00:31.250
the pre-festival day and
the main festival day.

00:31.250 --> 00:32.850
Uh-huh...

00:32.850 --> 00:35.270
Humans do very strange things.

00:35.270 --> 00:37.210
The dance festival, huh?

00:37.210 --> 00:40.560
Last year, we did a coffee 
shop, The Witch's House.

00:40.560 --> 00:43.360
Mama, are we gonna open 
the shop this year, too?

00:43.360 --> 00:45.030
Hmm...

00:45.390 --> 00:47.590
Should we?

00:56.610 --> 01:07.620
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

02:19.260 --> 02:21.990
Let's do it, Master!

02:22.210 --> 02:25.170
I want to do something 
even more fun this year!

02:24.000 --> 02:26.370
<b>We Opened the Coffee Shop Again This Year</b>

02:25.170 --> 02:28.120
Of course! And bring in even more profits!

02:28.120 --> 02:31.500
That's true. 
Our Witch's House coffee shop last year

02:31.500 --> 02:35.370
got a ton of customers thanks 
to all of our efforts...

02:36.070 --> 02:38.130
We truly are just that great!

02:38.130 --> 02:41.390
And Laika, everyone loved 
you in that uniform.

02:41.390 --> 02:44.880
Oh, please stop...

02:44.880 --> 02:48.890
But I also feel like it 
brought in <i>too</i> many people.

02:48.890 --> 02:52.640
Everyone was talking more about us 
than about the festival itself.

02:53.030 --> 02:54.760
Here's what I think.

02:54.760 --> 02:59.360
The reason our coffee shop is so popular 
is because it's only open once a year.

02:59.360 --> 03:01.660
That's exactly why people flock to it.

03:01.660 --> 03:04.920
Oh, yeah. That does make sense.

03:05.180 --> 03:08.910
So we should remove that 
novelty appeal from it.

03:08.910 --> 03:12.260
I suggest we make 
The Witch's House a permanent fixture.

03:12.260 --> 03:16.920
But that would mean we'd work at the 
coffee shop all the time, right?

03:17.250 --> 03:21.430
<i>This is going in the opposite direction 
from the slow life I wanted...</i>

03:21.930 --> 03:25.440
There's no need for anyone specifically 
in this family to work there.

03:25.440 --> 03:28.940
We could hire someone 
else to manage it, too.

03:29.220 --> 03:30.680
What a great idea!

03:31.080 --> 03:36.070
But is there anyone who'll agree 
to work for us that easily?

03:36.630 --> 03:39.680
I heard everything you just said!

03:40.020 --> 03:41.570
Misjantie?!

03:41.570 --> 03:46.450
Please allow me to be the 
manager of The Witch's House!

03:46.450 --> 03:48.360
We found one right away!

03:51.730 --> 03:57.170
Will your job propagating worship 
of the pine spirit allow for this?

03:57.170 --> 03:59.580
What will you do about weddings?

03:59.580 --> 04:01.760
I need to be multi-directional.

04:01.760 --> 04:04.930
Having followers isn't enough to 
put food on the table these days.

04:04.930 --> 04:07.110
<i>She's getting real!</i>

04:07.110 --> 04:10.050
So please let me do this, Azusa!

04:10.050 --> 04:13.980
I won't do anything to besmirch the 
good name of The Witch's House!

04:13.980 --> 04:18.030
All right. I'll put you 
in charge of it, then.

04:18.410 --> 04:20.870
Thank you so much!

04:20.870 --> 04:24.910
This year will see the opening of the 
coffee shop the House of the Pine Spirit!

04:24.910 --> 04:27.410
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

04:29.090 --> 04:30.410
That's a no!

04:30.410 --> 04:31.130
Huh?!

04:31.540 --> 04:36.560
It'll only work if the residents of the 
house in the highlands work there!

04:36.560 --> 04:39.540
I want to see you make a 
splash on festival eve day!

04:39.540 --> 04:41.620
This is what the whole village wants!

04:41.620 --> 04:47.300
Please... Please open The Witch's House 
at the festival again this year!

04:47.300 --> 04:51.050
Really? An offer directly from the village?

04:51.360 --> 04:54.180
Is that okay with you, Misjantie?

04:54.180 --> 04:56.200
It can't be helped.

04:56.200 --> 04:59.200
I can't compare to your record, 
not to mention your popularity.

04:59.500 --> 05:02.810
But if we get even more 
customers than last year,

05:02.810 --> 05:05.110
it could lead to pure chaos.

05:05.110 --> 05:07.070
And if that happens...

05:07.070 --> 05:10.460
The guild will hire adventurers 
to handle traffic control!

05:10.460 --> 05:12.940
Also, we'll use a numbered 
ticket admission system!

05:12.940 --> 05:17.450
But then you might have to deal 
with illegal ticket resales.

05:17.450 --> 05:21.580
We'll hire adventurers to watch 
for that so it doesn't happen!

05:21.820 --> 05:25.580
<i>She thinks she can get adventurers 
to take care of everything...</i>

05:25.990 --> 05:29.850
All right, then. Just one more time.

05:29.850 --> 05:31.930
Thank you so much!

05:32.690 --> 05:34.840
And that's the story.

05:35.220 --> 05:38.200
So we'll be opening the coffee 
shop again this year.

05:38.200 --> 05:40.850
Will you all help me out?

05:40.850 --> 05:43.450
Yay! I can't wait!

05:43.450 --> 05:45.120
I will work my hardest.

05:45.430 --> 05:48.230
Can't turn down a request 
from my big sister!

05:48.230 --> 05:50.110
You can count on me!

05:50.110 --> 05:52.830
I think I've grown a bit since then.

05:52.830 --> 05:55.500
Do you think I'll still fit in the uniform?

05:55.860 --> 05:57.150
<i>Is she bragging?!</i>

05:57.800 --> 05:59.710
Let's come up with a menu!

05:59.710 --> 06:00.990
And decorations!

06:00.990 --> 06:02.430
How about red?

06:02.430 --> 06:04.140
Sounds good!

06:04.140 --> 06:06.170
Laika, would you mind?

06:06.480 --> 06:10.800
Well, all right, if it's only for a day...

06:11.110 --> 06:12.600
Thanks!

06:12.600 --> 06:15.640
And Misjantie, you'll help us too, right?

06:16.670 --> 06:18.320
That just leaves...

06:19.210 --> 06:23.320
I'll pass. I don't like big crowds.

06:26.240 --> 06:29.950
<b>Then the Day Came</b>

06:30.740 --> 06:33.950
<b>Coffee Shop "The Witch's House" 
And a pine spirit, too!</b>

06:37.450 --> 06:40.990
It looks like the numbered 
ticket system was effective.

06:40.990 --> 06:44.590
And there've been no scalpers, 
thanks to the adventurers.

06:44.590 --> 06:47.680
I look forward to working 
with you all today!

06:48.080 --> 06:52.120
I'll be watching all of you and 
getting a good look at your talents!

06:52.120 --> 06:54.980
Good! Burn it deep into your mind's eye!

06:55.320 --> 06:57.730
It's nothing that special...

07:03.340 --> 07:06.390
I'll never get used to wearing this...

07:11.210 --> 07:13.010
Protect at all costs...

07:13.360 --> 07:16.000
You're taking this way too far!

07:16.000 --> 07:19.810
I won't complain if you can't give 
me very much attention today.

07:19.810 --> 07:21.620
Just do a good job.

07:24.670 --> 07:26.960
Welcome!

07:26.960 --> 07:28.760
Thank you for waiting!

07:28.760 --> 07:31.540
Our coffee shop, 
The Witch's House, is ope—

07:32.510 --> 07:35.840
Dear Sister, I've waited so long for this!

07:35.840 --> 07:38.630
We've come as customers this year.

07:38.630 --> 07:41.270
Why are you guys here?!

07:41.650 --> 07:47.460
We demons have taken on the role 
of livening up the dance festival.

07:47.460 --> 07:50.960
As payment, we have received 
the number 1 ticket.

07:50.960 --> 07:51.900
Uh-huh!

07:51.900 --> 07:53.950
So you're getting staff privileges!

07:54.480 --> 07:57.910
Wait, what does 
"livening up the festival" mean?

07:58.190 --> 07:59.850
You'll find that out...

07:59.850 --> 08:04.040
to-mor-row!

08:04.040 --> 08:05.930
More importantly, Dear Sister,

08:05.930 --> 08:10.520
how much do I need to pay to get you to 
write "I Love Pecora" on my omelet rice?

08:10.520 --> 08:12.840
This isn't that kind of shop.

08:12.840 --> 08:15.180
Just take your seats already.

08:15.180 --> 08:17.070
We'll show you to your table!

08:17.070 --> 08:18.430
This way.

08:18.430 --> 08:21.910
Oh, my daughters are so adorable!

08:21.910 --> 08:24.590
Go on, show us the way!

08:24.590 --> 08:26.380
I swear...

08:26.780 --> 08:29.830
Okay, the next customer can come in now.

08:30.220 --> 08:31.870
Welco—what?!

08:32.280 --> 08:34.400
How goes it? Makin' bank?

08:34.400 --> 08:37.710
Wait, ya only just opened up!

08:37.710 --> 08:41.110
Your Majesty, inventing your own joke

08:41.110 --> 08:44.070
when there is nothing to joke 
about is a breach of etiquette.

08:44.440 --> 08:47.080
Mu and Nahna Nahna are here, too?

08:47.420 --> 08:51.840
The demons allowed us to 
have the number 2 ticket.

08:52.460 --> 08:54.830
Hey, Mu! You came to see us?

08:54.830 --> 08:56.770
Yeah, I sure did!

08:56.770 --> 09:01.410
I said I didn't wanna, 
but Nahna Nahna just insisted!

09:01.410 --> 09:02.480
I did not.

09:02.480 --> 09:04.620
Good comeback!

09:05.470 --> 09:07.910
Well, shall we knock back some drinks?

09:07.910 --> 09:11.730
Your Majesty, that is a rather 
vulgar turn of phrase.

09:12.010 --> 09:14.870
Knock back all you like! Right this way!

09:14.870 --> 09:16.740
Great, thanks!

09:18.120 --> 09:21.800
I can't believe people we know 
got the first two tickets.

09:21.800 --> 09:24.310
Makes me wonder if some deals 
went on behind the scenes.

09:24.910 --> 09:26.870
Anyway, for real this time!

09:27.460 --> 09:28.380
Welco—

09:29.740 --> 09:32.880
Azusa! I'm here!

09:33.170 --> 09:35.260
You too, Momma Yufufu?

09:35.560 --> 09:37.330
This certainly looks fun.

09:37.330 --> 09:39.990
Your momma is happy to 
help you anytime, okay?

09:39.990 --> 09:42.770
You don't need to go that far.

09:42.770 --> 09:44.630
Looks pretty good, doesn't?

09:44.630 --> 09:46.770
It sure does!

09:47.140 --> 09:49.620
Okay, you can order whenever you're ready.

09:49.620 --> 09:51.880
All right. Thank you.

09:51.880 --> 09:54.170
Hey, um, Azusa...

09:54.170 --> 09:55.020
What?

09:55.390 --> 09:57.590
Could you take a look over there?

09:58.540 --> 10:01.900
Huh? Did we have a table there?

10:01.900 --> 10:03.540
Wait, what?!

10:03.540 --> 10:06.490
Azusa! Hi there!

10:06.490 --> 10:09.540
I invited Nintan, too!

10:09.540 --> 10:13.080
You didn't get a ticket before 
coming in here, did you?!

10:13.080 --> 10:14.510
You're breaking the rules!

10:14.510 --> 10:17.370
Numbered ticket rules are for humans.

10:17.370 --> 10:19.270
Gods have no need for them.

10:19.270 --> 10:21.340
So don't worry!

10:21.340 --> 10:24.220
We brought this table in ourselves.

10:24.220 --> 10:26.800
Nobody else can see it!

10:26.800 --> 10:29.070
That's not the problem here!

10:29.070 --> 10:31.680
Bringing in your own accommodations 
will get you banned!

10:31.980 --> 10:34.560
But the customers are gods.

10:34.560 --> 10:36.820
You just wanted to say that!

10:55.380 --> 10:57.580
What? Taking a break?

10:57.580 --> 11:00.870
Yeah. Everyone's doing 
their job really well.

11:00.870 --> 11:04.480
I see. Sounds like you're 
all doing just fine.

11:04.480 --> 11:05.720
Huh.

11:06.800 --> 11:12.690
Yeah, but honestly, it'd be a huge help 
if we had one more helper, y'know?

11:12.990 --> 11:16.680
What is that? Are you asking me to help you?

11:16.950 --> 11:21.650
I can't. I mean... I don't 
have a uniform or anything.

11:21.650 --> 11:24.240
I'd look weird among all the others.

11:24.840 --> 11:26.030
Sandra.

11:27.350 --> 11:30.520
I made one for you, too!

11:30.520 --> 11:32.130
Will you help me?

11:34.170 --> 11:36.840
W-Well, I suppose I have no choice.

11:36.840 --> 11:40.140
I'm willing to help you 
out just a little bit.

11:44.240 --> 11:45.830
Who's that little kid?

11:46.290 --> 11:48.380
The up-and-coming new face around the shop!

11:48.690 --> 11:51.500
She's carrying dishes she 
isn't used to carrying!

11:51.500 --> 11:52.900
Careful, now!

11:56.960 --> 11:58.560
Sorry for the wait.

12:48.840 --> 12:51.450
Thank you very much!

12:55.120 --> 12:56.960
<b>Closed</b>

12:57.280 --> 12:59.390
Thanks for your help, too, Misjantie!

12:59.390 --> 13:01.330
You were a lifesaver!

13:01.620 --> 13:03.970
No need to thank me.

13:03.970 --> 13:06.070
I'm gonna use what I learned here

13:06.070 --> 13:09.710
to make the House of the
Pine Spirit coffee shop a reality!

13:10.840 --> 13:13.480
Good work today, Dear Sister!

13:13.840 --> 13:17.100
Pecora! Didn't you go home?

13:17.100 --> 13:21.230
I'm not going home. 
There's still tomorrow, after all.

13:21.230 --> 13:22.670
Tomorrow?

13:23.390 --> 13:26.500
Oh, you did say you were doing 
something at the dance festival.

13:26.830 --> 13:29.480
You'll see what it is tomorrow.

13:40.550 --> 13:43.590
Are they plotting something again?

13:44.510 --> 13:48.010
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

13:48.050 --> 13:51.510
<b>The Day of the Dance Festival</b>

14:08.440 --> 14:12.320
I'm with Dear Sister! I'm with Dear Sister!

14:12.320 --> 14:15.780
Dear Sister, I'm so excited 
for the festival!

14:15.780 --> 14:17.580
<i>It's so hard to walk like this.</i>

14:17.580 --> 14:20.780
Azusa, walk a little bit slower.

14:20.780 --> 14:21.700
Okay, okay.

14:21.960 --> 14:26.080
No, Dear Sister. Why don't 
we pick up the pace a bit?

14:26.340 --> 14:29.810
What's your deal? Azusa is walking with me!

14:29.810 --> 14:31.140
Rawr!

14:31.140 --> 14:33.970
Oh, dear. Is the baby in 
her rebellious phase?

14:34.310 --> 14:37.810
I bet your seed leaves are just 
starting to sprout, aren't they?

14:37.810 --> 14:39.510
Excuse me?!

14:40.170 --> 14:43.520
Cut it out, you two. 
We're here for the festival.

14:44.160 --> 14:45.630
Actually...

14:46.730 --> 14:49.490
Doesn't it seem like there 
are a whole lot of stalls?

14:49.910 --> 14:51.740
And they're all run by demons.

14:52.030 --> 14:54.250
We're using Flatta as a test case

14:54.250 --> 14:58.270
for building harmony between 
demons and humans.

14:58.270 --> 15:00.970
And they're bringing life to the 
festival. A good idea, right?

15:00.970 --> 15:02.970
So that's what you meant.

15:02.970 --> 15:05.420
Well, it seems fun, so I guess it's all good.

15:09.990 --> 15:11.880
What cute dolls!

15:12.220 --> 15:15.310
This is terribly intriguing.

15:17.340 --> 15:20.530
Attention, everyone!

15:19.930 --> 15:22.280
I know that voice...

15:20.530 --> 15:25.600
Eno, the Witch of the Cave, is here to 
introduce to you these Mandragora Pills!

15:25.600 --> 15:29.030
They've saved the life of the 
Witch of the Highlands herself!

15:29.030 --> 15:29.700
Sneak, sneak!

15:30.000 --> 15:32.830
If you're from Flatta, you've gotta buy some!

15:33.320 --> 15:34.450
I knew it.

15:34.920 --> 15:36.290
Oh, Eno!

15:36.290 --> 15:39.000
Azusa! It's been a while!

15:40.970 --> 15:42.830
Rawr! Rawr!

15:42.830 --> 15:44.900
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

15:44.900 --> 15:47.340
I won't try to catch you anymore!

15:47.880 --> 15:50.340
Sandra, calm down.

15:50.670 --> 15:52.860
Did the demons invite you, too?

15:52.860 --> 15:57.110
Yes, Beelzebub asked me if 
I wanted to run a stall.

15:57.110 --> 16:00.600
It seems she's invited many others, as well.

16:00.600 --> 16:02.830
Oh, really?

16:02.830 --> 16:05.960
This is the game corner!

16:05.960 --> 16:07.850
That can only mean...

16:07.850 --> 16:11.240
The tournament will begin in ten minutes!

16:11.240 --> 16:14.870
We have prizes, too! Be sure to take a look!

16:15.590 --> 16:17.610
I thought it was you, Pondeli!

16:18.400 --> 16:21.390
Azusa! It's good to see you again!

16:21.390 --> 16:25.000
Please feel free to try out my latest game!

16:26.700 --> 16:30.010
Give it all you've got, both of you!

16:30.010 --> 16:31.240
Very well.

16:31.240 --> 16:34.640
Red Dragon's Blazing Roar!

16:34.640 --> 16:36.290
That's nothing!

16:36.290 --> 16:39.150
Blue Dragon's Freeze Breath!

16:45.010 --> 16:46.430
What is that?!

16:46.430 --> 16:50.120
A competitive card game 
that uses ancient magic.

16:50.120 --> 16:54.380
Looks like I didn't get the 
fine tuning quite right.

16:54.380 --> 16:56.040
This goes way too far!

17:17.980 --> 17:21.840
I see this area is set up like a market.

17:25.350 --> 17:26.190
Ugh...

17:26.190 --> 17:27.440
What <i>are</i> these?

17:27.440 --> 17:28.860
What's going on?

17:36.820 --> 17:39.120
Oh! Curalina!

17:39.540 --> 17:40.620
Here you go.

17:44.950 --> 17:46.720
Is this...

17:46.720 --> 17:49.560
...what we look like?

17:50.100 --> 17:52.840
That doesn't really fit 
the whole festival mood.

17:55.490 --> 17:57.130
Look, Mama!

17:57.130 --> 17:59.450
Beelzebub bought them for us.

17:59.450 --> 18:01.390
Oh, how nice!

18:01.390 --> 18:05.260
Of course! I'll buy you as many as you want!

18:05.550 --> 18:07.010
I swear...

18:07.270 --> 18:11.220
Lady Azusa, this dance 
festival truly is fun!

18:11.220 --> 18:15.020
Yeah. I'm glad we all got 
to come together again.

18:15.020 --> 18:17.950
I heard there's a concert starting 
on the special stage soon.

18:17.950 --> 18:20.490
Yeah, I heard it's this amazing singer!

18:20.780 --> 18:22.690
The only singer I know is...

18:23.120 --> 18:24.790
Kuku, maybe?

18:25.290 --> 18:28.370
Well, it's been ages. 
Let's go listen to her.

18:28.800 --> 18:34.660
<i>Ki-ki-ki-ki-killer sparkles, 
and so colorful!</i>

18:34.930 --> 18:37.750
<i>Shame is a companion to madness</i>

18:37.750 --> 18:39.600
<i>Roughly, greedily</i>

18:39.600 --> 18:41.010
<i>Pour it on! Spill it over!</i>

18:41.410 --> 18:44.350
<i>Flowers only bloom in 
darkness, minute by minute</i>

18:41.690 --> 18:42.940
Oh, it's Pecora.

18:44.350 --> 18:47.310
<i>Here in hell, where we celebrate it</i>

18:47.310 --> 18:50.360
<i>Bursting straight from the soul</i>

18:50.360 --> 18:53.800
<i>And you can always come back for more</i>

18:53.800 --> 18:56.800
<i>Sometimes you get your hopes up too 
high and end up betrayed, right?</i>

18:56.800 --> 19:00.950
<i>To avoid that hassle, all you need 
to do is keep your eyes on me!</i>

19:00.950 --> 19:03.750
<i>I'll fulfill everything you're 
wishing for in that brain of yours!</i>

19:03.750 --> 19:07.240
<i>The happiness of demonkind will make 
all people so happy they could die!</i>

19:07.580 --> 19:09.150
<i>Here we go!</i>

19:09.150 --> 19:13.250
<i>The sickness is made up of hope and dreams</i>

19:13.250 --> 19:16.250
<i>Keep stanning me until your 
life comes to an end</i>

19:16.470 --> 19:21.600
<i>Have fun singing the chorus 
that pours from your body</i>

19:21.600 --> 19:24.900
<i>With the kind of charm that turns</i>

19:24.900 --> 19:28.890
<i>everything into skull and heart marks</i>

19:28.890 --> 19:31.670
<i>Sing my praises until your throat bleeds,</i>

19:31.670 --> 19:38.110
<i>for all eternity</i>

19:38.110 --> 19:41.020
<i>Cuteness in full bloom! Everyone's 
obsessed with Demon King Pecora!</i>

19:41.940 --> 19:43.740
Look over here!

19:43.740 --> 19:45.600
Pecora rules!

19:45.950 --> 19:48.960
Thank you, everyone!

19:49.290 --> 19:52.870
That was Her Majesty Pecora, 
the beloved idol...

19:52.870 --> 19:55.830
...and Kuku the minstrel!

19:56.400 --> 20:02.920
Everyone, I'm here today to serve as 
a bridge between demons and humans!

20:04.840 --> 20:07.230
So as a part of that,

20:07.230 --> 20:10.350
I'd like to introduce 
someone very dear to me!

20:10.350 --> 20:12.360
Come on up here,

20:12.360 --> 20:15.350
my dear sister, the Witch of the Highlands!

20:15.630 --> 20:16.530
Huh?

20:17.350 --> 20:19.860
What?!

20:25.180 --> 20:26.620
Great Witch!

20:29.840 --> 20:31.760
Witch of the Highlands!

20:33.750 --> 20:35.430
Lady Azusa!

20:35.430 --> 20:37.030
Master!

20:37.030 --> 20:38.570
Is she going to be okay?

20:38.570 --> 20:39.840
Mama!

20:39.840 --> 20:42.310
I look forward to seeing what Mother does.

20:42.310 --> 20:44.190
Sister, you look great!

20:44.190 --> 20:47.010
Show everyone what you've 
got, whatever it may be!

20:47.940 --> 20:50.520
So it's Azusa's turn this time.

20:50.830 --> 20:54.010
I'm so happy to be appearing 
here with you, Dear Sister!

20:54.540 --> 20:57.490
So what am I supposed to do now?

20:57.490 --> 20:59.020
Well, of course...

20:59.350 --> 21:00.770
Sing!

21:00.770 --> 21:03.690
What?! No, no, I can't!

21:03.690 --> 21:05.900
Nice to see you again, Azusa.

21:05.900 --> 21:08.920
Do you mind if I accompany you?

21:08.920 --> 21:11.420
Kuku... You, too?

21:11.420 --> 21:13.870
Please sing, Great Witch!

21:21.180 --> 21:25.540
You are the very embodiment of 
a free spirit, you know that?

21:37.400 --> 21:42.770
<i>I pray again this year</i>

21:42.770 --> 21:48.490
<i>That we can continue to smile</i>

21:49.070 --> 21:53.740
<i>If the fields can be dyed 
the colors of the rainbow</i>

21:54.360 --> 21:58.870
<i>As far as the eye can see</i>

21:59.540 --> 22:03.570
<i>The little bird of happiness</i>

22:03.570 --> 22:10.640
<i>Flies high in the sky</i>

22:12.100 --> 22:17.390
<i>The four seasons</i>

22:17.390 --> 22:23.990
<i>Keep coming again and again</i>

22:23.990 --> 22:30.200
<i>This place where we've come to be reborn</i>

22:30.200 --> 22:35.330
<i>Is the hometown where the 
flowers of love bloom</i>

22:35.330 --> 22:40.540
<i>Abundant and healthy</i>

22:40.540 --> 22:45.800
<i>Give thanks to all that lives</i>

22:45.800 --> 22:52.510
<i>Ah, thank you</i>

23:16.330 --> 23:18.150
Master!

23:18.150 --> 23:19.700
You're so good, Mama!

23:19.700 --> 23:21.280
Not bad at all!

23:21.280 --> 23:22.510
I'm so moved.

23:22.510 --> 23:23.860
Lady Azusa!

23:23.860 --> 23:25.180
That was great!

23:25.180 --> 23:27.350
Sister, you're the best!

23:30.350 --> 23:32.950
Thanks, everyone!

23:34.980 --> 23:39.980
<b>Thank you for watching!</b>
